# The source corpus is NOT in Git-LFS. It moved to a yidam artifact vault (epic #2141, #2147):
# `data/*/*/vault.yaml` records which bytes exist, R2 holds them at their content address, and
# `watermark documents hydrate` restores a working tree. The globs that used to bind
# data/documents/** and data/reference/** to LFS are gone — the set they described now lives in
# `watermark.documents.vault.VAULTED_SUFFIXES` and in the generated block in `.gitignore`.
#
# What survives here is the chain-of-custody rule that has nothing to do with LFS: the source
# bytes that DO stay in the repository must never be line-ending-normalized.

# Captured web evidence (HTML/text): preserve the exact response bytes, including CRLF line
# endings — never normalize a source byte under data/documents (chain of custody). Small
# enough to stay in the repository, unlike the vaulted scans.
data/documents/**/*.html -text
# Also covers the derived `<dir>-text/` sidecars (#1757) — small UTF-8 transcriptions of the
# vaulted legacy binaries, committed like the captured evidence above.
data/documents/**/*.txt -text
# The sanitary production's native web/markup formats stay raw bytes like .html/.txt.
data/documents/**/*.htm -text
data/documents/**/*.HTM -text
data/documents/**/*.xml -text

# The published USGS low-flow appendix CSVs are the publisher's own files, committed as served
# (CRLF line endings and all) — never a re-export. Preserve the exact response bytes, same rule
# as the captured web evidence above; they are small, so not LFS.
data/reference/usgs/low-flow/*.csv -text

# ── GitHub Linguist ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep the repo's language stats about the actual CODE (the Python backend + the Astro
# frontend), not the corpus, the vendored design mirror, or generated artifacts — and
# collapse the regenerable/data diffs by default so PRs stay navigable. These attributes
# only affect GitHub's display + language bar; they change no git, build, or LFS behavior.

# The public-records corpus + authoritative reference datasets are primary source DATA,
# not code. Exclude the YAML/JSON/Markdown/HTML/CSV evidence from language stats (the
# vaulted binaries are not in the repository at all).
data/** linguist-vendored

# The committed content-bundle fixtures are generated (trimmed) by `bosc export`.
frontend/sample-bundle/** linguist-generated

# The design system is a mirror of the Claude Design "Watermark" project, pulled via
# DesignSync (vendored specs + ui_kits, not hand-authored app code) — keep its
# jsx/ts/html/css out of the stats. (tsconfig already excludes it from type-checking.)
frontend/design-system/** linguist-vendored

# The docs tree is documentation, not a programming language.
docs/** linguist-documentation

# Generated artifacts regenerated by a `bosc` command — collapse their diffs too.
docs/HYDROLOGY.md linguist-generated
docs/COMPUTE.md linguist-generated
data/catalog/COMPLETENESS.md linguist-generated
data/catalog/**/README.md linguist-generated

# Lock files are generated (package-lock.json is auto-detected; uv.lock is not).
uv.lock linguist-generated
